    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite consists of just `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are an abstract base and a helper). It passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag on owner creation, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern end-to-end.\n\n**Behavior:** When a create's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (case-insensitive), the created owner is returned with `capacityWarning: true`. Below 40 it's `false`; the hard rejection at **50** (409 Conflict) is unchanged.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant; extracted the per-city count into a shared `countOwnersInCity(...)` helper used by both the hard-limit check and the new `isApproachingCityCapacity(...)` helper; `addOwner` now computes the city count once, enforces the limit, and sets the warning flag before saving.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the DDL; added to all dialects for consistency).\n\nThe target test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` (fills a city to 40, then asserts the 41st owner warns) passes, and the full suite is green.",
